<section style="padding:96px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Nobody on the Avalon publishes oil tank prices, so most people call around and get a "we'll have to come look" from everyone. That's fair for the tricky jobs, but for a standard outdoor tank swap the numbers don't move much, and you deserve to see them before you pick up the phone. Here's what oil tank replacement costs in Newfoundland in 2026, based on published Atlantic Canada retail pricing, all in CAD.</p><p>The short version: a new 200-gallon steel tank installed, with your old tank hauled away, runs about $3,200. A fibreglass or Roth double-wall tank is about $3,850, and a smaller 100-gallon tank for heat-pump backup is around $3,100. Those figures include the HOST inspection and registration, so the tag on your new tank is part of the deal, not a surprise line on the invoice. If you'd rather skip the reading and get a number for your own house, <a href="/oil-tank-replacement-st-johns/">ask for a free written estimate</a> and we'll get it to you quickly.</p></div></div></section>
